data.content:
## What breaks in .NET 11

In EF Core 10, the Cosmos DB provider deprecated synchronous LINQ operations (`ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()`, etc.) but offered an opt-in flag (`CosmosOptionsExtension.EnableSyncExecution`) to keep them working temporarily.

**In EF Core 11, that opt-in is removed entirely.** All synchronous LINQ query operations on the Cosmos DB provider now throw `InvalidOperationException` unconditionally. There is no workaround short of switching to async.

## What you must change

Every sync LINQ call must become its async counterpart:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key points:**

- `ToList()` → `ToListAsync()`
- `First()` → `FirstAsync()`
- `Count()` → `CountAsync()`
- `SaveChanges()` → `SaveChangesAsync()`
- All callers up the stack must also become `async`/`await`
- Remove any `EnableSyncExecution` configuration — it no longer exists

`Add()` remains synchronous (it's an in-memory tracking call, not a query), so that line stays as-is.
